  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Don't pre-populate Remote Interfaces with recent data",
  "description": "The rpcap data in recent_common lists (all) rpcap hosts that\na user has connected to. There's no guarantee that all of them\nwill still work, and get_remote_interface_list() tries to make\na connection to each, which takes a *long* time to timeout for\nany that don't work. Any that require a username and password\ndon't work, because we don't store that information (see the\nsimilar issue with extcap).\n\n\"rpcap interfaces to connect to at startup\" has to be saved\nseparately, presumably in a preference file, from \"[all] recent\nrpcap interfaces we know about.\"\n\nThe user already has to open up \"Manage Interfaces\" to get these\nto populate; for now, they'll have to add them each time (though\nat least the combobox in RemoteCaptureDialog will remember the old\nones and suggest them and pre-populate port and auth type.\n\nRelated to #17484. Reopen #8557.",
